 * from lexer.js.
 *
 * Precedence, loosest to tightest: comparisons, then `+`/`-`, then `*`/`/`,
 * then `^`, then a leading unary `+`/`-`. Comparisons and the additive and
 * multiplicative operators group to the left; `^` groups to the right, and
 * binds looser than a leading sign (so `-2^2` parses as `(-2)^2`).
 *
